<para id="RM00000064G00IX" category="J" type-id="300WK" name-id="5915C-00" from="200708">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>Cruise control switch circuit</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM00000064G00IX_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000C9D00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>The cruise control main switch outputs the power switch signal for cruise control and the signals of each operation switch to the engine control computer.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>The engine control computer performs cruise control according to the signals from the switch.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000064G00IX_02" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000C9E00000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E143509J01" width="7.106578999in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000064G00IX_03" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___0000C9F00000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten3>
<ptxt>When the engine control computer is replaced with a new one, be sure to perform initialization. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000002GO2003X"/>)</ptxt>
</atten3>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM00000064G00IX_04" type-id="01" category="01">
